WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.110
The Marvel Cinematic Universe has a lot of
extremely powerful characters.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.740
Hey, they're superheroes after all.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.020
Being super powered is just part of the whole
deal.

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.950
And fans love to debate just who is the most
powerful of them all.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.820
Is it Thor, the god of thunder and heir to
Odin's legacy?

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.560
"Strongest Avenger."

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.600
"Access denied."

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.780
"STRONGEST AVENGER."

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:19.780
"Access denied."

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.120
Is it the incredible Hulk, whose strength
scales with his nearly limitless anger?

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.580
Is it Hawkeye, who can shoot an arrow real
good?

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.310
Actually, it turns out that the correct answer
is none of the above, because there's one

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.590
Marvel legend who goes higher, further, and
faster than the rest of Earth's Mightiest

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.080
Heroes.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.920
Yes, people, it's official canon: Marvel Studios
president Kevin Feige has confirmed that the

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.449
most powerful hero in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe is Captain Marvel.

00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:49.399
"She's one of the most powerful, and one of
the most popular characters in our comics,

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.520
and will be the most powerful character in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe"

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.280
Feige explained that it took a while to get
to the point where the time was right to finally

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.440
introduce Captain Marvel to movie fans.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:05.290
"Captain Marvel is a character in our comics,
and in the mythology, who's got one foot on

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.080
Earth and one foot in the cosmic arena.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.680
So before she could be introduced the whole
cosmic side of things have to be explored

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.440
in movies like Guardians of the Galaxy and
Thor: Ragnarok.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:19.940
"Now that we've made a number of movies that
take place on Earth, and now a number of cosmic

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:24.290
adventures... we thought it was the right
time to finally introduce Captain Marvel to

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:24.860
the world."

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.560
This isn't the first time he's said it, either.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.409
Way back in 2016, not long after star Brie
Larson was cast as Captain Marvel, Feige told

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:33.500
Vulture the same thing.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.540
"It's very important to us that all of our
heroes do not become silhouette-perfect cutout

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:38.040
icons.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.780
All of the Marvel characters have flaws to
them [and] all of them have a deep humanity

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:42.360
to them.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.159
With Captain Marvel, she is as powerful a
character as we've ever put in a movie.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:50.479
Her powers are off the charts, and when she's
introduced, she will be by far the strongest

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.600
character we've ever had.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.920
It's important, then, to counterbalance that
with someone who feels real.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.280
She needs to have a humanity to tap into,
and Brie [Larson] can do that."

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.720
Fans saw both sides of Captain Marvel on full
display when the film hit theaters on March

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.560
8, leaving no doubt that Larson's hero is
now the strongest one in the MCU.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.680
And that has fans speculating about what that
might mean when she teams with the surviving

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.860
members of the Avengers for Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.190
The newest trailer for Avengers: Endgame featured
Captain Marvel, wearing civilian clothes and

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:22.050
looking a bit older than she did in her 1995-set
standalone movie, hanging around at Avengers

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:22.580
HQ.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.460
This sequence seemed to directly follow the
mid-credits scene in Captain Marvel, which

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.720
saw her return to Earth and ask the Avengers
where Nick Fury was.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.860
And that, of course, indicated that she had
indeed received the desperate page Fury sent

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.660
out in the post-credits scene of Avengers:
Infinity War.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.290
He wanted some help fighting off Thanos.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.800
Well, looks like he got his wish!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.660
Of course, exactly how Captain Marvel's presence
will affect the balance of power in the fight

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:47.810
against Thanos remains to be seen, but considering
the bearer of the Captain Marvel name has

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:52.380
long been Thanos's arch-enemy in the comics
and considering the fact that Feige has confirmed

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.670
that Carol Danvers is the strongest one there
is, all we can say is, sorry Thanos!

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.160
Time's up.

